  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Propanol (propyl alcohol) is used as an antiseptic and disinfectant for the skin. It is an approved topical antiseptic, though it is not an authorised medicine in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q14985&quot;>Wikidata Q14985</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>propanol</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D08AX03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB03175&quot;>DB03175</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/1031&quot;>1031</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q14985&quot;>Q14985</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C3H8O</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>60.096 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
